data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

**EF Core 11 completely removes synchronous I/O for the Cosmos DB provider.** The `.NET 10` opt-in (`CosmosOptionsExtension.EnableSyncIO`) no longer exists — calling any sync API **always throws** at runtime with no workaround.

**All four of your methods break:**

| Method | Issue | Fix |
|--------|-------|-----|
| `ToList()` | Throws | `await ToListAsync()` |
| `First(...)` | Throws | `await FirstAsync(...)` |
| `Count()` | Throws | `await CountAsync()` |
| `SaveChanges()` | Throws | `await SaveChangesAsync()` |

**Required fix** — convert to async:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

This is a **source-breaking** change — there is no opt-in flag or compatibility shim in EF Core 11. All callers of these methods must also be updated to `await` the results, propagating `async` up the call chain.
